      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>XIII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.23"/> Gif mon oðres wudu bærneð oððe heaweð unaliefedne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.24"/>, forgielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.25"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.dagger"/> ælc great treow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.26"/> mid V<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.10"/> scill., ⁊ siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.27"/> æghwylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.28"/>, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.14"/> swa fela<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.29"/> swa hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.30"/> sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.14"/>, mid V pæningum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.31"/>; ⁊ XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.32"/> scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>XIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.1"/> oþres wudu bærneð oþþe heaweþ unalyfedne, forgylde ælc great treow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.8"/> mid V scll', ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.1"/> siþþan ælc, swa monig swa þær sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.4"/>, mid V peningum; ⁊ XXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Be wudebernete, ⁊ gif man afylled bið on gemænu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> weorce. Gyf man oðres wudu bærneð oððe heaweþ unalyfedne, forgylde ælc great treow mid fif scill', ⁊ syþþan æghwylc, sy swa feola swa heora sy, mid fif penegum; ⁊ þrittig scill'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.star2"/> to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis nemus alterius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.26-2"/> sine licentia comburat uel taliet, soluat omne grossum lignum quinque solidis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.27-2"/>, deinceps omne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.28-2"/>, quotquot sint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_12.lnote.oe.29-2"/>, quinque denariis restituat, et triginta sol. wite, id est forisfacti.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="70" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be wudebernete, ⁊ gif man afylled bið on gemænum weorce.] Gif mon oðres wudu bærneð oððe heaweð unaliefedne, forgielde ælc great treow mid V scill., ⁊ siððan æghwylc<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Af_12.attnote.fn.16"/>, sie swa fela<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Af_12.attnote.fn.17"/> swa hiora sie<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Af_12.attnote.fn.18"/>, mid V pænigum<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Af_12.attnote.fn.19"/>; ⁊ XXX scill.<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Af_12.attnote.fn.20"/> to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="14" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="308" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XIII} Gif mon oðres wudu bærneð, oððe heaweð unaliefedne, forgielde ælc great treow mid scill, ⁊ siððan æghwylc, sie swa fela swa hiora sie, mid V pæningim; ⁊ XXX scill to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand das Gehölz eines anderen ohne Erlaubniss abbrennt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.2"/> oder abhaut, so vergelte er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.3"/> jeden grossen Baum mit 5 Schill., und weiterhin jeden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.4"/>, sei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.5"/> es so viele als ihrer seien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.6"/>, mit 5 Pfennigen; und 30 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.7"/> zur Strafe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_12.lnote.de.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone burns or cuts down another’s woodland without permission, let him pay for each large tree with 5 shillings, and after that for each one, however many of them there may be, with 5 pence; and 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="71" ed="#attenborough"/>If one man burns or fells the trees of another, without permission [to do so], he shall pay 5 shillings for each big tree, and 5 pence for each of the rest, however many there may be; and [he shall pay] 30 shillings as a fine<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_12.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If a man burns or fells the wood of another, without permission, he is to pay for each large tree with five shillings, and afterwards for each, no matter how many there are, with fivepence; and 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="309" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a someone burns another’s wood or cuts it down without permission, let him compensate for each large tree with 5 shillings, and afterwards each [smaller tree], however many there may be, with 5 pennies; and 30 shillings as fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43-1">Ine 43.1</ref> <quote>there are differences in the sums levied for ... felling another's trees (n. 72: Af 12, Ine 43:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="299"><label>emends</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43">Ine 43</ref> <quote>Ine §44 stipulates that a man must pay 30 shillings for each of the first three trees [...] Alfred §14 requires only a 5-shilling payment</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43">Ine 43</ref> <quote>Contrast with Ine §44 where different fines are established for felling or burning another's wood. These clauses suggest that Ine's laws were [...] superseded</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43-1">Ine 43.1</ref> <quote>Ine §44.1 requires the first three trees felled to be recompensed with 30 shillings each</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="51"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43">Ine 43</ref> <quote>Some appear to have furnished inspiration … [n. 31:] See, for example, Ine §44 (on burning a tree), Alfred §14.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="409"><ref target="clause:Ine_43-1">Ine 43.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor c.</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">stellt So:</hi> 18 — 18, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So places 18 — 18, 3 before cap. 12</seg></note>
