        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.oe.29-2" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">supersunt <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supersunt Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i<hi rend="italic">d est</hi> half pund <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 12. <hi rend="italic">Jh. übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i<hi rend="italic">d est</hi> half pund written above in the 12th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vor c. 12 stellen So Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>: c. 18—18, 3 als sinnverwandt, über Unzucht an Nonnen. — ‘Und wenn ein Mensch bei gemeinsamer Arbeit erschlagen wird’ fügt B der Rb hinzu, aus Af 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Before c. 12, So Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> place c. 18—18, 3, on unchastity with nuns, as related in subject. — B adds to the Rb ‘And if a man is killed during common work’, from Af 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Baum 5; roden 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Baum 5; roden 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht liess Archetyp eine Zahl (wie eine in Ine 43, 1 steht) aus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps the archetype omitted a number (such as stands in Ine 43, 1)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H modernisiert. — Im Ggs. zu Ine wird, trotz einheitlicher Strafe, der Tatbestand für die Busse zersplittert; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 119</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H modernises. — In contrast to Ine, the offence is split up for the purposes of compensation, despite a uniform fine; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 119</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Turk interpungiert hinter <hi rend="italic">sic:</hi> ‘jeder sei mit 5 Pf.’ — unmöglich. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> vielmehr Ine 43, 1 <hi rend="italic">wære hiora swa fela swa hiora wære</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Turk punctuates after <hi rend="italic">sic:</hi> ‘let each be at 5 pence’ — impossible. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> rather Ine 43, 1 <hi rend="italic">wære hiora swa fela swa hiora wære</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘viele’ mit sg. verbi</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘many’ with sg. of the verb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">30 Sch. erklärt als 1/2 £ B cor., für Af falsch, nach Mercischem Schilling (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 6) rechnend, weil Schreiber in oder nahe London lebte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">30 shill. is explained as 1/2 £ by B cor., wrongly for Af, reckoning by the Mercian shilling (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6), because the scribe lived in or near London</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_12.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 5</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>æghwylc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ælc</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>fela</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">feola</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>sie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swa monig swa þær sy</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>pænigum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">penegum</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">peningum</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>scill</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">id est half pund</hi>. 12th century addition to B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_12.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The explanation (in B) <hi rend="italic">id est half pund</hi> is incorrect. The scribe was reckoning in Mercian shillings which contained four pence. The West Saxon shilling at this period contained five pence (cf. note to Ine, cap. 59).</seg></note>
      </div>
